{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwukqKv71D1LAjstjaLE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I estimated the ATT with inverse-propensity weighting. I fit a logistic regression of treatment `t` on `x0`–`x16`. I then weighted each control by e/(1−e), where e is the control's propensity score, and compared the treated mean of `y` with the weighted control mean.\n\nThe raw difference in means is negative (treated 0.772 vs. control 0.861), but controls are not comparable to the treated. After adjusting for the confounders, the effect is positive.\n\nOther adjustments gave similar results:\n\n| Method | ATT estimate |\n|---|---|\n| Inverse-propensity weighting (reported) | 0.0726 |\n| Regression adjustment (outcome model fit on controls, applied to treated) | 0.0694 |\n| OLS with a treatment dummy | 0.0645 |\n\nThe estimate is about 0.073, meaning training raises the outcome `y` by roughly 7 percentage points among the treated.\n\nANSWER: 0.073"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":30871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3b144df-33b0-4ffb-94a8-be9b1bb20436","uuid":"2da102f1-f5fc-4072-9306-0922bb2b283f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:13:50.653Z","request_id":"req_011Cgwukq4J8uuh9d2NRuCTd"}
